    "solution": "From the smoke, parry a bolt right through the still-empty casting frame into the distant coil. That opens the home door and the lower carriage route, but home is still exposed to the watch light. Drop onto the broad carrier and ride beneath the gale and the thorn floor to the far side. Jump onto the wide anvil pedestal and land before using a small jump and downward cut. Its rebound reaches the high gallery above the same thorn and projectile lane. Follow the gale into the sheltered shaft, let yourself settle beside the mould, and strike left to cast both parts of the screen. Jump left over the new low wall; the central gust carries you across the gap to the starting smoke. Walk home through the screen’s long shadow.",
    "nearestExisting": "B29 combines transported shade with a returned shot, B30 casts shade during a swing, and B12 replaces a temporary shield. Here a shot can cross the gale that prevents the knight from reaching the casting face. Its coil releases both the lower carriage and the home door; a lower ride and upper anvil return approach the same frame from its useful side before the final walk uses its permanent shadow.",
    "novelty": "The shared passage has three different uses at three heights: a bolt travels upwind through the empty frame, a carrier takes the knight below the thorn-covered firing lane, and the anvil returns the knight above that same lane into the casting pocket. Only then can the frame become the screen needed for the long downwind home route.",
